I cannot reproduce the reported outage between PC4 and Laptop0. Current evidence shows Layer-3 connectivity is healthy across the access switch and inter-VLAN gateway:

- From PC4 (172.16.10.4/24, gw 172.16.10.1) to Laptop0 (172.16.20.10/24, gw 172.16.20.1): 0% loss, ~1.27 ms RTT (pc4 -> laptop0 ping successful). Reverse direction from Laptop0 to PC4 is also 0% loss, ~1.12 ms RTT.
- Both hosts have correct IP and default gateway configuration (verified via ip addr/route on pc4 and laptop0).

Mechanism and localization: The traffic path PC4 -> switch1 -> mswitch1 -> router0 (gateway between 172.16.10.0/24 and 172.16.20.0/24) -> back to switch1/mswitch1 to Laptop0 is functioning normally. The successful bidirectional ICMP, low RTT, and proper default routes confirm forwarding and ARP resolution are intact on the involved devices and interfaces.

Root cause: No persistent fault found; the issue appears transient or host-specific and is not present now.

Corrective fix: No changes required. Recommend the user retest. If the problem recurs, capture details at the time of failure (ping/traceroute from PC4, arp -n, and the output of ip addr/route), and note whether Laptop0 was asleep or its link was flapping to help isolate an intermittent host or link condition. === END ===